.TH TASKHEALTHD 8 "August 2026" "TaskHealth 0.2.1" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
taskhealthd \- Linux user-space thread health monitoring daemon
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B taskhealthd
[\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B taskhealthd
is a standalone daemon that monitors the health of threads across multiple
user-space processes.  Client applications register their threads and report
heartbeats over a Unix domain socket; the daemon watches those threads for
unexpected exit, futex deadlock, and lock-wait timeouts using
.I /proc
probes, and emits alerts when a fault is detected.
.PP
The monitoring unit is the thread (TID), not the process.  Registration is
keyed by \fI(pid, tid)\fR, so heartbeat, exit, deadlock, and lock-wait
detection all target individual threads.
.PP
.B taskhealthd
runs in the foreground by default.  Use
.B \-\-daemonize
to detach, or run it under systemd (a
.I taskhealthd.service
unit is provided).
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-s ", " \-\-socket " " \fIPATH\fR
Unix domain socket path to listen on (default: \fI/tmp/taskhealth.sock\fR).
.TP
.BR \-i ", " \-\-interval " " \fIMS\fR
Watchdog scan interval in milliseconds (default: 1000, clamped to
100\-60000).
.TP
.BR \-m ", " \-\-max\-entries " " \fIN\fR
Maximum number of monitored threads (default: 4096, clamped to 1\-65536).
.TP
.BR \-d ", " \-\-daemonize
Detach and run in the background.
.TP
.BR \-a ", " \-\-alert\-script " " \fIPATH\fR
External script invoked with alert details (default: none).
.TP
.BR \-l ", " \-\-log\-file " " \fIPATH\fR
Append alerts to \fIPATH\fR (default: syslog only).
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print a usage summary and exit.
.SH DETECTION
.B taskhealthd
detects three classes of fault:
.TP
.B Unexpected exit
A registered thread terminates without calling the client's unregister
function.
.TP
.B Deadlock
A thread whose heartbeat has timed out is blocked on a futex (its kernel
wchan shows \fIfutex\fR).
.TP
.B Lock-wait timeout
A thread remains blocked on a futex longer than its configured lock-hold
threshold.
.PP
When the client library reports the futex address before blocking and the
mutex was registered with a name, alerts resolve the blocked address to a
human-readable lock name.
.SH ALERTS
Alerts are emitted by severity.  Critical alerts (unexpected exit, deadlock)
are printed to stderr and recorded to the log; lock-wait alerts are recorded
to the log only.  Output targets are syslog, the optional
.B \-\-log\-file ,
and the optional
.B \-\-alert\-script .
.SH SIGNALS
.B taskhealthd
terminates gracefully on
.BR SIGTERM ,
.BR SIGINT ,
or
.BR SIGQUIT ,
stopping the watchdog and closing the socket.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /tmp/taskhealth.sock
Default Unix domain socket.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR taskhealth (7),
.BR taskhealth-demo (1)
